{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097704-scions-of-titans","id":1097704,"title":"Scions of Titans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-27T23:54:13-07:00","id":1097704,"title":"Scions of Titans","content":"Silly question but can the Titans create scions? dark scions? evil scions? They were gods at one point themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T00:23:20-07:00","id":1097706,"title":"","content":"It has been hinted at in 1st ed, but nothing about what we know about 2e rules it out. We don't have a lot of info on the differences between them, mechanically yet. Known differences between Titans and Gods in 2e are scale (may have changed) and virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T00:37:13-07:00","id":1097707,"title":"","content":"There're plans to have rules for Titan-born Scions in 2e in a supplement, with separate Callings and Knacks that cause physical deformities.<br /> <br /> Scions who fight <i>alongside</i> the Titans take on their Virtues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T00:40:19-07:00","id":1097708,"title":"","content":"We know Titans are more defined by specific Purviews than Gods, and may lack Callings altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T01:49:30-07:00","id":1097714,"title":"","content":"While nothing too certain has been said, my personal logic is that since the Titans mainly differ from the Gods by their lack of humanity they wouldn't be able to have a &quot;human&quot; scion in their current state without giving up what makes them titanic in the first place, although adoption might be an option if you can persuade them to care.<br /> <br /> That said, in my games it's totally possible that they'd sire/create inhuman scions, and any number of frost giants/centaurs/kitsune/whatever might be running around claiming to have the ichor of greater powers running through their veins...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13499,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","user":"Not Quite Yoda","date":". 05-28-2017, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:42:57-07:00","id":1097735,"title":"","content":"I preferred the idea that Titans can create Scions, but Gods are just much more inclined to doing so with humans then titans are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T05:16:21-07:00","id":1097753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Not Quite Yoda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097704-scions-of-titans?p=1097714#post1097714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While nothing too certain has been said, my personal logic is that since the Titans mainly differ from the Gods by their lack of humanity they wouldn't be able to have a &quot;human&quot; scion in their current state without giving up what makes them titanic in the first place, although adoption might be an option if you can persuade them to care.<br /> <br /> That said, in my games it's totally possible that they'd sire/create inhuman scions, and any number of frost giants/centaurs/kitsune/whatever might be running around claiming to have the ichor of greater powers running through their veins...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not so sure that's the case. If Titans were incapable of having human(ish) children, then we wouldn't have the Gods and the world would still be under their rule. The fact that these forces of nature were able to give birth to creatures of intellect and reasoning indicates that such Scions are entirely possible. Heck, they might even have greater potential than regular Scions, since they're 'first generation' and all.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, Fate will not have a direct influence in shaping your existence as a mythical being; it simply builds itself around your established identity. That means the Gods would have been humanoid prior to founding their legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-28-2017, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T10:54:48-07:00","id":1097825,"title":"","content":"So it might be possible to have a scion of a titan instead of one who has turned to serving them ... interesting ... evil ideas forming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T12:04:55-07:00","id":1097838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097704-scions-of-titans?p=1097825#post1097825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it might be possible to have a scion of a titan instead of one who has turned to serving them ... interesting ... evil ideas forming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Indeed, I'm really excited for the possibility of playing a Scion level character who's not strictly human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But the way I see it, the difference between Titans and Gods is their intentions. <br /> <br /> Titans have no great plan; they flex their power simply because they have the freedom to do so. They just want to do whatever makes them happy at the time.<br /> <br /> Gods, on the other hand, use their powers for some sort of purpose, interacting with society and guiding it towards whatever goal they have planned, be it for good or ill.<br /> <br /> <br /> In other words, you have the Chaos vs Order dichotomy in regards to which is which.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-28-2017, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T06:34:59-07:00","id":1098089,"title":"","content":"They have shown ways to be various kinds of mythical being rather than a demigod of otherwise human descent. Hell, one of those is a talking dog. No reason a Titanspawn PC would be out of reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:43:11-07:00","id":1098146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097704-scions-of-titans?p=1098089#post1098089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have shown ways to be various kinds of mythical being rather than a demigod of otherwise human descent. Hell, one of those is a talking dog. No reason a Titanspawn PC would be out of reach.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Where have they shown this? I want to check it out! &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T18:07:51-07:00","id":1099344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097704-scions-of-titans?p=1098146#post1098146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Where have they shown this? I want to check it out! &lt;3</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFor some reason I can't seem to find that talking dog. It was the Irish black dog, hound of the Tuatha, I can't remember the name. But they also have satyrs, deer women and hulder in the April preview. I expect building a Titanspawn wouldn't be that much different: Set relationships, path skills and knacks. A Manticore probably has an innate ranged attack with Piercing and Lethal, as one example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:15:24-07:00","id":1099478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097704-scions-of-titans?p=1099344#post1099344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bFor some reason I can't seem to find that talking dog. It was the Irish black dog, hound of the Tuatha, I can't remember the name. But they also have satyrs, deer women and hulder in the April preview. I expect building a Titanspawn wouldn't be that much different: Set relationships, path skills and knacks. A Manticore probably has an innate ranged attack with Piercing and Lethal, as one example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I heard once or twice that inanimate objects can also be chosen for Scions, which I'm assuming is something along the lines of Galatea in which a sculpted woman is brought to life. If this is true, then it gives me an idea for a Scion of a forge god who poured their heart and soul into their craft, inadvertently bestowing it with a portion of their divinity and granting it a life of its own. I'll wait for 2nd edition to elaborate more clearly on the mechanics before I describe anything in more detail, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T21:50:16-07:00","id":1100006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097704-scions-of-titans?p=1097825#post1097825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it might be possible to have a scion of a titan instead of one who has turned to serving them ... interesting ... evil ideas forming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also want to point out that in 2E, the Titans will apparently not be exclusively antagonistic like they were in 1E.<br /> <br /> Meaning that you could potentially have the children of Gods and Titans working together; although not without tension, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-04-2017, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}